<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abba-El I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abba-El I was king of Yamhad, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, in the 18th century BCE. After putting down a revolt in the city of Irridu, he destroyed it and gave his brother Yarim-Lim the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alalakh">Alalakh</a> in exchange, creating a dependent kingdom there. The grant is recorded on a tablet found at Alalakh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abba-el-i.jpg" alt="Abba-El I" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attar-Aram syria · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abba-El_I_seal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
